From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jake Cattrall <krazyjakee@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:10:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Repaint only the damaged part of a frame (vello_cpu over
 softbuffer)

ImageRenderer gains supports_region and render_region: render the pixels
of a region into a full-size image and leave the rest. vello_cpu renders
the scene shifted into a region-sized context (kept while the size
repeats) and copies it in; the result is pixel for pixel what a full
render gives there.

SoftbufferWindowRenderer implements supports_damage and render_damage
with it: it keeps the last frame, repaints the damage into it, converts
only that rectangle when the surface's buffer holds the last frame
(buffer age 1), and presents it with present_with_damage. Without a GPU
an animation then costs its own rectangle, not the window.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
